## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/clamp.html
- Summary (EN): The Clamp node restricts the values of a layer, VDB or attribute to an optional lower and upper range. Values outside the range are replaced by the exceeded limit or by zero, or softly transitioned with Soft Clip.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Clamp borne les valeurs d'une couche entre une limite basse et une limite haute, avec remplacement par la limite ou par zéro, ou transition douce par Soft Clip.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: the layer, VDB or attribute to clamp", "lower (optional): per-pixel scale for the lower limit", "upper (optional): per-pixel scale for the upper limit (the page text says lower limit, which looks like a typo)", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Mask: how much of the clamped result is mixed in, default 1", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels affected", "Compute Range: sets Lower and Upper Limit to the source min and max", "Lower Limit / Upper Limit: thresholds, with a dropper to pick values from the layer", "Clamped Values: Replace with Limit Value, or Replace with Black (0)", "Soft Clip: smooth transition instead of a hard cutoff", "Soft Clip Direction: transition inside or outside the range", "Soft Clip Range: width of the transition"]

- Caveats: ["The Upper input description says lower limit; treated here as upper-limit scaling", "Soft Clip changes values near the limits, so a hard clamp and a soft clip give different results"]

